  ],
  "text": "The calcium in your bones was made inside a star that exploded before the Sun existed. The Big Bang made almost nothing. Hydrogen, helium, and a trace of lithium. That is the entire list. No carbon. No oxygen. No iron. No calcium. Everything heavier had to be built afterwards, and there is only one place hot enough. Inside stars. Fusion squeezes light elements into heavier ones, step by step, over billions of years. Carbon. Oxygen. Silicon. All of it assembled in a core nobody could ever see into. But a star cannot make anything past iron. Past iron, fusion costs energy instead of releasing it. So the heaviest things came from the deaths. Supernovae, and neutron stars colliding. The iron in your blood. The calcium in your bones. The oxygen you just breathed in. You asked what you are made of. This is the answer. Things that had to die first. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
